\title{The topological branch: drawings to additive blocks}
\taxon{Overview}
\meta{dependencies}{None.}
\meta{provenance}{Expository organization and source review, 9 October 2026.}

\p{This branch explains how an arbitrary continuous drawing yields [the block relation](cn-0018). [Normalization](cn-0009) makes local geometry manageable. Signed interior intersections alone omit contributions at common endpoints; the half-order terms restore the cycle identity. Definitions are [drawings](cn-0003), [crossings](cn-0004), [normalization](cn-0008), [signed intersections](cn-0010), [spoke orders](cn-0011), [cycle vectors](cn-0012), and [the corrected matrix](cn-0013).}

